{
  "id": "armour",
  "description": "Wearable armour. Adding a piece is one entry here: its slot supplies the equip slot and the body parts it hides, its material supplies the stat tier. The builder reads which biped slots a mesh actually occupies out of the NIF itself, so nothing about coverage is hand-declared. `meshes` gives one base path per sex WITHOUT the _0/_1 weight suffix: the builder ships _1 geometry with _0 as a morph target and the runtime blends by the wearer's body weight (decision 0056). The path is declared, never inferred — Bethesda uses four different conventions for the male/female split (iron/male + iron/f; studded/male + studded/female; elven/m + elven/f; steel root + steel/f; and bare suffixes for dwarven ...f, orcish cuirassm/cuirassf, daedric daedriccuirass/daedrictorsof). A base with no _0/_1 pair (both iron helmets, both orcish helmets) ships as a single mesh with no morph target.",
  "outputDir": "output/armour",
  "iconDir": "output/armour-icons",
  "manifestOutput": "output/armour.items.json",
